# Keys for the widgets that need one. Copy this file to .env (which git and
# Docker ignore) and fill in your own. The keys stay on the server: the dev
# server and the Docker image's nginx add them to requests, and the page never
# sees them. Leave one empty and its widget says it isn't set up.

# AI Leaderboard: a data key from https://data.benchlm.ai/account
BENCHLM_TOKEN=

# Popular TV: the "API Read Access Token" from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
TMDB_TOKEN=

# Agenda: your Google Calendar. Calendars can be added in the Agenda widget's own
# settings, each with a name and a description, with no need to restart anything.
# Calendars set here are the server's own: every visitor sees them, and their
# addresses never reach the page or a YAML export.
#
# In Google Calendar, open a calendar's settings (Settings, then the calendar
# under "Settings for my calendars"), scroll to "Integrate calendar" and copy the
# "Secret address in iCal format". Anyone with that address can read the calendar,
# so keep it here, never in git. Resetting it in Google Calendar makes the old one
# stop working.
#
# The dashboard shows what is in the calendars to anyone who can open it, so keep
# it behind your VPN or your reverse proxy's login if it can be reached from
# outside your home.
#
# The server can hold up to three calendars, each in its own colour. Leave the
# ones you don't need empty.
CALENDAR_ICAL_URL=
CALENDAR_ICAL_URL_2=
CALENDAR_ICAL_URL_3=
